Weekly new-business leads: <%= @total_new %> new <%= "lead".pluralize(@total_new) %> this week.

<% @sections.each do |section| -%>
== <%= section[:source].tr("_", " ").upcase %> ==

<% if section[:failed] -%>
Fetch failed; no data was recorded this week. Check the production logs for "[LeadGen]". Missed businesses will surface in next week's run.
<% elsif section[:seeded] -%>
First run: seeded <%= number_with_delimiter(section[:sighted_count]) %> register entries. Nothing is reported as new on a seed run; next week's digest will carry the first real leads.
<% elsif section[:new_leads].empty? -%>
No new businesses this week.
<% else -%>
<% section[:new_leads].first(LeadDigestMailer::TABLE_ROW_CAP).each do |lead| -%>
- <%= lead.business_name %> | <%= lead.business_type %> | <%= lead.postcode %> | <%= lead.local_authority %>
<% end -%>
<% if section[:new_leads].size > LeadDigestMailer::TABLE_ROW_CAP -%>
...plus <%= section[:new_leads].size - LeadDigestMailer::TABLE_ROW_CAP %> more in the attached CSV.
<% end -%>
<% end -%>

<% end -%>
